given:
  - Location = "Loop"

# Two `choice:` blocks below share the exact same label ("Go on"), so they compile to the same
# child situation (`begin::loop::go-on`) -- the compiler namespaces a choice's own body by its
# parent rule plus a slug of its own label, and a later definition for the same slug silently
# wins (`ravel.utils.data.merge_dicts`). That's deliberate here: this fixture exists to give
# `encode_save`/`engine.resume` two choice blocks with an identical `anchor.choices` tuple in one
# situation, disambiguated only by `ordinal` (data-model.md SS Choice blocks, anchors, and saved
# frames). Only "Second time through." ever actually runs; "First time through." is dead body
# text kept for readability, not a bug.
loop:
  - when:
      - Location = "Loop"
  - You are looping.
  - choice:
      - [Go on]First time through.
  - effect: Visited = 1
  - choice:
      - [Go on]Second time through.
